          "date": "2026-11-06 05:04:37.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-06 05:04:37.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: fewer remote commands in setupall checks",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: fewer remote commands in setupall checks\n\nsanity_mount_check() ran one remote command per server\ntarget and one per client mount point, 15 for a DNE\nconfiguration of 4 MDTs and 8 OSTs. Check all server mount\npoints on all server nodes in one command, and both client\nmount points in another.\n\nload_modules() ran load_modules_local() through rpc.sh on\nevery remote node even when the modules were loaded, and\nrpc.sh costs about a second to start. On nodes where\nlustre.ko is loaded and the udev rule load_modules_local()\nwrites is in place, only reset the debug masks as it would,\nin the same remote command. A node with an older test\nframework that does not write the rule is loaded as before.\n\nMeasured on a cluster of one MDS with 4 MDTs, one OSS with 6\nOSTs and 2 clients, median of 3 to 6 runs, as is and with\n0.25 s added to each remote command:\n\n                      cmds      as is           +0.25 s\n  sanity_mount_check 13 -> 2  1.01 -> 0.23 s  4.10 -> 0.71 s\n  load_modules        1 -> 1  1.22 -> 0.34 s  1.41 -> 0.56 s\n\nWith the two changes before this one, setupall went from 164\nto 37 remote commands, 23.3 to 17.7 s as is and 41.6 to\n22.8 s with 0.25 s added.\n\nCI runs about 220,000 setupalls and 750,000 load_modules()\ncalls with the modules loaded in 30 days. At the savings\nmeasured above (0.78 to 3.39 s per sanity_mount_check and\n0.85 to 0.88 s per load_modules), that is 48 to 207 hours and\n177 to 183 hours, so about 230 to 380 hours of test time.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity,sanity-quota\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ib30f0524619e8a5e8000cdcbcf33985efdc980d1\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
